.TH PROXCHUNKD 1 "2026-08-21" "proxchunk 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proxchunkd \- proxy fetch and score daemon for proxchunk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proxchunkd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B proxchunkd
.B \-\-foreground
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B proxchunkd
.B \-\-stop
.br
.B proxchunkd
.B \-\-status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proxchunkd
fetches public HTTP and SOCKS5 proxy lists, scores them, and leases
live endpoints to
.BR proxchunk (1)
over a UNIX socket.
.PP
With no arguments the process daemonizes.
The parent exits 0 when the socket is listening; the first score pass
may still be running.
.B ACQUIRE
retries until a live proxy is free (or 30 s elapse on the client).
.PP
Already running (socket
.B PING
works): start is idempotent, prints
.B already running
on stderr, and exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Stay in the terminal.
Ctrl+C, SIGTERM, and SIGQUIT perform a graceful stop.
The libsf proxy progress bar is drawn on the initial refresh when
stdout is a TTY; later refreshes are quiet.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Ask the daemon to shut down (STOP on the socket, then SIGTERM to the
pidfile if needed).
Idempotent: already down exits 0.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Ping the socket and print
.B live
/
.B busy
/
.B top_mbps .
Exit 1 if not running.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
UNIX socket.
Default:
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/proxchunk/proxchunkd.sock
(fallback
.IR /tmp/proxchunk-$UID/proxchunkd.sock ).
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " path"
PID file (default: sibling
.IR proxchunkd.pid ).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-proxies " " \fIN\fR
Maximum live proxies to keep (default: 40).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-refresh " " \fIsec\fR
Re-test interval in seconds (default: 180).
.B 0
disables the updater thread.
.TP
.BI \-\-test\-url " url"
Scoring URL
(default:
.IR https://speed.cloudflare.com/__down?bytes=65536 ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not load or save
.IR ~/.cache/proxchunk/proxies.txt .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tor
Do not auto-add local Tor on port 9050/9150.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fetch
Do not fetch public proxy lists (tests / offline).
.TP
.BI \-\-socks " url"
Extra HTTP or SOCKS proxy.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy\-file " file"
Load extra proxies, one
.I ip:port
or URL per line.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-user\-proxies
Do not load
.IR ~/.config/proxchunk/proxies.txt .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Log file when daemonized
(default:
.IR ~/.cache/proxchunk/proxchunkd.log ).
In
.B \-\-foreground
logs go to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print
.BR proxchunkd " " 1.1 .
.SH IPC
Line-oriented UTF-8 on a
.B SOCK_STREAM
UNIX socket, max 4096 bytes per line.
The first command must be
.BR "HELLO 1" .
.PP
.B ACQUIRE
is non-blocking:
.B OK
.I url mbps
or
.BR "ERR empty" .
The client retries.
On disconnect, held URLs are released as failures so busy leases cannot leak.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/proxchunk/proxchunkd.sock
Control socket (mode 0600; directory 0700).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/proxchunk/proxchunkd.pid
PID file with an exclusive
.B fcntl
lock.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/proxchunk/proxies.txt
Scored proxy cache.
.TP
.I ~/.config/proxchunk/proxies.txt
Optional user proxy list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, already running, help/version, or idempotent
.BR \-\-stop .
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, failed start, or
.B \-\-status
when down.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR proxchunk (1),
.BR curl (1)
.SH AUTHORS
proxchunk contributors.
